"DIALOGUE.oarfish.birthdayGift.winter.20": "[220]...$h#$b#%Oarfish smiles knowingly at you. She hunched her back and pantomimes watering flowers.",
"DIALOGUE.oarfish.birthdayGift.winter.23": "[196]...$h#$b#%Oarfish smiles knowingly at you. She held an invisible palette and drew brushstrokes on an invisible canvas.",
"DIALOGUE.oarfish.birthdayGift.winter.26": "[605]...$h#$b#%Oarfish smiles knowingly at you. She wore a depressed look and starting hammering on an invisible anvil.",







// ***** [MARR] MARRIAGE DIALOGUE *****
// Remi Marriage Dialogue
"MARRIAGE.remi.patio": "Feels nice out here on the patio.$9#$b#I wish I could see what your farm looks like. Fish tells me it fits your personality.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.funLeave": "I'll be going somewhere.#$b#Dunno where I'll end up, but I'm sure it'll be something... or nothing.#$e#Either way, I'll have fun for sure.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.funReturn": "[346 394 257 259]I'm home! Here's a souvenir for ya.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.jobLeave": "Gonna do some errands today. You do what you gotta do.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.jobReturn": "I'm back. Had a productive time. You?$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spouseRoom": "I don't really know what my room looks like, but it sure feels comfy.$11",

"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.1": "The air feels really nice when it rains.$9#$e#I just wanna snuggle on a warm body and do nothing all day.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.2": "[730]This is good to eat on a rainy day, trust me. Dig in.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.3": "Going out in this weather? At least wear a raincoat so we don't worry about you.#$e#But I'm sure you'll be fine. You're built different.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.4": "Water's dropping from the sky. That means less work for you, right?#$e#So, what do you do when the rain takes care a part of your workload?#$b#More work?$6#$b#...$6#$b#Well, you do you.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.5": "The soil outside smells nice right now.$u#$e#I just really love the smell of petrichor.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.6": "Gonna work in the rain? Don't catch a cold, y'hear?#$e#Do you even get sick?$6#$e#Ah well, better that than being sick, right?$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_day.7": "[730 732]Here's something to fill you up quick.#$e#Feels humid around here. Is it raining?$6#$e#Yep. It's raining. Watch your step out there.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.1": "Welcome back. Here's a towel. Rub yourself dry.#$e#Hm? Oh, me and Fish are fine. Day well spent.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.2": "You're wet. I'll fetch you a change of clothes.#$e#So how did your day go?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.3": "[236 231]I prepared something hot tonight. It's pretty good to eat in a weather like this.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.4": "Can't really hug you when you're drenched.#$b#So get yourself dry soon, okay?$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.5": "$c 0.5#You smell like petrichor. I love it.$11#I wonder how my sewer friend is doing? I know he loves the rain.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.6": "You're wondering how I'm able to cook, right?#$b#There are such things as blind chefs. And my nose is unparalleled when it comes to sniffing out the best flavors.#$e#Fish helps me out, too.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.rainy_night.7": "Feels real nice to sleep during this weather.$9#$b#I think I'm gonna tuck in soon.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.1": "Good morning.#$b#...Is it morning?$6#$b#[201 215 240]Yep. It's morning. Enjoy your breakfast.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.2": "$c 0.5#Oh, hey. You started moving. That means it's morning, right?#Hey, thanks for letting me use the kitchen. Don't worry about the ingredients. Fish and I have our ways.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.3": "[204 226 732]It's your lucky day! Here's some grub.$9#$b#Go get 'em, tiger.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.4": "Mmmm... smells good. What's cooking?$u#$b#Oh wait, I'm cooking.$6#$e#[201 215 240]When I say I'm forgetful, I mean I'm reaally forgetful. Here's your grub.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.5": "Fish told me it's morning.#$b#She also wanted me to tell you she greeted you good morning.#$e#Although she did that while you're still asleep. Silly gal.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.6": "[265]I tried something different in the kitchen today.#$b#This one will get you into a real fishing kick for sure.$9#$e#Have I told you I love fishing? Odd since I don't like the deep waters, but it's my favorite thing to do back then.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_day.7": "*Yaaawn*, is it morning? Can't really tell.$6#$b#[201 215 240]Anyways, here's breakfast. Have a good day out there.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.1": "Good work out there. Now get some well-deserved rest.#$b#What? Want me to tuck you in? Hehe.$11#$e#I'd actually do that if you want me to by the way.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.2": "[236 244 205 729 213 235]Tonight's special. Dig in.#$e#So, tell me about your day.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.3": "$c 0.5#Yeah, I can cook. My nose leads me to the tastiest outcomes. I have Oarfish help me with the knifework, though.#Have I told you about that weird smell coming from the backwoods?$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.4": "$c 0.5#You smell sweaty. Worked hard, huh?#Hey, I prepared the bath ahead of time. You smell like you need it.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.5": "Air feels cooler. Good evening.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.6": "I feel like tucking in soon. You should, too.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.indoor_night.7": "I'm guessing it's nighttime. Feels cooler out.#$e#Wanna tell me the details about how your day went? Maybe over dinner?$9",

"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.1": "It doesn't matter if people can see me.$6#$b#The moment they look away, I am forgotten.$6#$e#It got its pros and cons.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.2": "You really love working, huh?#$b#I can waft a bit of your scent everywhere out here.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.3": "Just doing my thing out here.#$e#You know what's great? The fact that you're always so busy working out there that Fish and I can- er...$11#$e#Nothing. Nevermind.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.4": "What's up?#$e#Me? I'm good. Fish, too.#$e#Yeah, I got nothing much to say today. But standing out here feels great.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.5": "Got a recipe to suggest for later? I'm down to experiment, too.#$e#Hmm... you think I make too much seafood? Well, it's my favorite.#$e#Maybe something with kale? ...Nah.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.6": "I can't really see what your farm looks like, but it's yours so it gotta be good.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.outdoor.7": "Hey! Come and stretch with me out here for a bit!$h#$e#Oh right, you're always breaking your back out there working.#$b#We appreciate the work you do, just wanted to say.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.OneKid.1": "Your kid pinched my finger. So cute.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.OneKid.2": "Aha, your kid got tiny hands.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.OneKid.3": "You think the kid needs a playmate?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.OneKid.4": "Never thought I'd be raising a kid, never thought I'd enjoy it either.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.TwoKid.1": "Your kids are getting along, thankfully. The house is a lot smellier now.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.TwoKid.2": "Smells poopy around here sometimes, but that's what happens when you got kids.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.TwoKid.3": "They smell like you, which is good. I don't have to cringe at the awful human smell too much.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.TwoKid.4": "Kids have really strange desires...#$b#Some too disturbing to let anyone else know.$6",

"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.1": "How's my favorite, least smelliest person?$9#$e#If you need my help just let me know, okay?#$e#Fish is here for you, too.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.2": "[346 394 257 259]Fish and I had our midnight walk a few days ago. I forgot to hand you this souvenir.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.3": "[346 459 303 348]Hehe, I haven't lost my magic touch. Enjoy.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.4": "I love you!$9.#$b#Thought that might perk you up. I mean it, though.#$e#Fish loves you, too.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.5": "It's really comfy here. I don't regret crashing in with you at all.$9#$e#Really, I mean it. Thanks for everything, @.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.6": "$c 0.5#I'm in the mood to show off some culinary skills. Request me anything.#Hey uh, don't be shy if you want a hug, or if you want to hug me for no reason. Some simple contact is good for your sanity, as they say.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.7": "Ehehehe...$u#$e#I'm just really happy. Don't mind me.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.8": "Want me to help you out? I'm down.#$e#I can't do much of visual work, though. Gotta be something I can feel around to.$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.9": "Hey, hey. Stand still for a bit, will ya?#$b#%*hug*#$b#There. Off you go.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Good.10": "Good work out there.#$e#I know I say that a lot, but I sincerely appreciate the work you do around here.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.1": "I wonder what your grandpa smell like?#$b#What? Too weird?$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.2": "You good? Me? I'm okay.#$e#Fish is okay, too.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.3": "If you feel like heading to the mines, don't hesitate to tag one of us along.#$b#Doesn't hurt to have a backup, and we could use the exercise.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.4": "Nice crib. Just wanted to say.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.5": "Feeling... neutral.#$b#At least that's what Ms. Luck Lady says for me, according to Fish.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.6": "Lucky day? Unlucky day? What does it matter?#$b#The day is in your hands.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.7": "What recipes do you know? Thinking about exchanging notes.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.8": "Dunno what to do for the day... maybe I'll lounge around.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.9": "I'm down for some conversations.#$e#So, what topic do you like?#$e#I know I said I can read desires, but I can never be exactly sure what YOU desire. You surprise me sometimes, even.$11#$b#So, instead of making assumptions, I think it's nicer to just ask you.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Neutral.10": "Sorry if I repeat myself sometimes. I got a bad memory.$6",

"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.1": "You're starting to smell awful. Dunno why.$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.2": "...you're boring.$7",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.3": "You're bored of me, aren't you?$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.4": "Get lost.$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.5": "Kinda wanna go back to the railroads...$7",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.6": "...$a",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.7": "Can't deal with you right now. Don't you got work to do?$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.8": "...sigh.$s",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.9": "Don't wanna hug you.$7",
"MARRIAGE.remi.Bad.10": "You make me sad.$7",

"MARRIAGE.remi.NoBed.1": "The floor doesn't feel nice to sleep on...$7",
"MARRIAGE.remi.NoBed.2": "Sigh... I miss a comfy bed.$s",
"MARRIAGE.remi.NoBed.3": "I patted around everwhere and there is no bed. Where did it go?$s",
"MARRIAGE.remi.NoBed.4": "I feel really groggy. Need bed.$s",

"MARRIAGE.remi.spring": "The cherries smell lovely at this time of year.$11#$e#Fish tells me how the cherry tree petals have the same color as my skin.#$e#Is that a good thing?$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer": "Fish sometimes tell me about fireflies. If only I could witness them.#$e#I'm not really bitter about being blind, though. I'm fine with the way I am.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall": "The season smells like crimson and gold. Fantastic.#$e#Yeah, I can sort of smell colors.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter": "It's really cold even with my coat on. Ah well.",

// Remi Seasonal dialogue for events said in marriage
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.1": "Smells like spring. Which means a whole year has passed.#$b#So what's your resolution?#$e#Haha, I'll try to remember. You better do something about that this year, though!$h",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.2": "Y'know, Oarfish's hobby is looking over at the calendar and preparing something nice for whoever's having their birthday soon.#$b#Problem is, she never got the courage to just walk up to someone and hand 'em a gift. So I do that for her.#$b#Spooks people out, though. I mean, they couldn't remember where the gift came from.$6#$e#...So, you down to do the gift giving this year? Fish would really appreciate it.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.8": "Lots of work to do now that winter's over. That means you're gonna get sweatier, huh?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.15": "You smell that? It's gonna be a free-for-all with all these berries ripe for the picking.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.23": "Flower dance, eh? Fish and I are too old for that.#$e#Go to the dance tomorrow, though.#$b#Me and Fish got... other plans. Hehe.$12",

"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.15": "A lot of things smell so new and fresh this season.$9#$b#Like the wonderful scent of life springing out of the ground after being trapped under the cold for so long.$11#$e#Huh, is that exactly what's happening?$10#$b#Hm! Must be a beautiful thing to witness, then.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.9": "Can't believe I'm saying this, but I love this planet.$11#$b#Getting past the smell, there's lots of fun to be had here.#$e#...hehehe, mommy was right.$u",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.12": "Tomorrow's Egg Festival? Yeah, no thanks. Fish and I don't go to human events.#$e#You know me. I don't like the smell.$11#$b#And Oarfish, well... she's shy.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.19": "Do you smell that?#$b#Smells like... %favorite.#$e#What? Isn't that what you desire most?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.spring.27": "Arcade night!$9#$b#Not that I can play any of the games, but just listening to Oarfish's turbulent desires is plenty entertaining enough for me.#$e#So, think you can beat Fish's high score?$12",

"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.1": "Feels hotter than usual. Guess it's summer.#$e#That means more flies, and cold summer treats.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.8": "You're a lot sweatier than usual. Lucky you don't smell too human, huh?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.15": "Some tiny things are landing on me.$7#$b#Flies? Yeah flies.$6",

"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.11": "The luau, huh?#$b#A single whiff and I'll know exactly what that vat of soup needs.$11#$b#Although you can never go wrong with good-quality cauliflower.#$e#You think you can bring home some for us? Or do only attendees get a taste?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.22": "Is it... Sunday?$6#$b#No- Monday. It's Monday.$10#$e#Sorry if I threw you off. I know how important time is to you.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.16": "My eyes are in two different colors? I didn't know that.$6#$e#Are eyes supposed to look the same?#$b#Well, I figured most bodies of living beings are symmetrical, so that makes sense.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.12": "So, do you always do something that involves %favorite or...?#$e#You don't have to elaborate if you don't want to.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.27": "Tonight's saloon night. Join us if you want. I'll even get you something from the menu.$11#$e#I'd gladly spoil my friends. Especially when I can only have so few in the span of eternity.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.21": "Hoo-wee! Another hot week.$11#$b#Ice cream sure is a great pleasure this season.#$e#By the way, did you know you can buy ice cream even without its vendor?#$b#Fish went around the counter and I \"bought\" the ice cream.$11#$e#I'm sure you can figure out how to get another living being to stand behind the counter, too.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.summer.28": "Moonlight Jellies viewing?$6#$b#We're good.#$e#Fish probably had plenty of encounters with ocean-life at the beach already.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.1": "Feels crunchy outside. Probably fall.#$e#By the way, the start of fall is Fish's birthday.#$e#I already got something for her later. But feel free to treat her with something nice.$11#$b#She'll appreciate it for sure.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.8": "It's getting chilly now. Wear something thicker, y'hear?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.15": "Grange display? I can't do much of anything about any sort of display, but oh well.#$e#Fish is willing to help out, though. Have I told her she has an eye for style and color? They say she's quite the artist. Wish I could see 'em...$11#$e#Anyways, good luck tomorrow. We're rooting for ya.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.26": "Spirit's Eve, huh? You go on your own.#$b#Me and Fish got other ways to spend the night. Heh.$12#$e#Here's a tip. Some things are not what they seem.#$b#And when that happens, you gotta feel around the walls.$11",

"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.22": "I don't hate humanity or anything. I just can't stand their odor for too long.$6#$e#If a human is in danger and I can do something about it, I'd gladly rescue them. But that's about it.#$e#Besides, it's not like they'll remember me.$7",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.9": "Fish and I will eat out at the saloon.#$b#See us this evening if you can. We'll get a third seat for you.$11#$e#On that note, what's your favorite meal?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.19": "Sorry if this is a stupid question but...$6#$b#is %favorite something you can eat in this planet?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.20": "I'm not sure if the ordinary human can smell it, but you smell a lot like the forest magic that permeates this valley.$11#$e#It's why I can stand you. Besides you being able to see and remember me and all that.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.7": "I don't remember if I told you about her yet... it's not Fish.$7#$b#She's a really good friend from back home. I love her so much.#$e#...$s#$b#Oh, sorry. I'm tearing up a little thinking of her. Haha.$9#$e#I know she still remembers me. Because I still remember her.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.fall.27": "Ooooh, spooky times.$11#$b#I'm not into dressing up, though. But, the pumpkins smell great.#$e#Fish would love this time of the year, now if only her pranks aren't so... extreme. Hehe.$11",

"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.1": "Brrrr... Getting really cold now.$10#$b#Hehe, that just means I'll snuggle more than usual.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.7": "Fishing contest? Make me proud.#$e#[265]Maybe this dish can help.#$b#Eat it before entering the forest, though. Don't want others to catch you getting a boost.$12",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.25": "Heh, you think I'd forget? Here's a present for you.[279]#$e#Been a great year, huh? We love you, @.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.28": "The year is ending soon. I can smell spring from just around the corner.#$e#Thanks for making it a good one. Me and Fish had a blast living another year with you.$9",

"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.22": "I never would've bothered coming to Earth, honestly. The way humans smell is already a huge dealbreaker for me.$7#$e#But here I am. Me and Fish against the rest of the world... except it's not like that anymore.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.12": "%favorite!!!$h#$e#Hehehe, what? I just yelled what you desire most.#$b#Things I say are forgotten anyways, if that makes you feel any better.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.6": "You ever wanted to borrow my coat or something?#$b#You know, for warmth. It's pretty chilly out.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.winter.21": "Looks like all those weeks of talking to you and giving you gifts paid off. We're best buds now!$h#$e#...What?#$b#Oh right, of course your talking and gift-giving to me are also part of why I'm very fond of you.$11#$e#It's really nostalgic... like how the three of us were back home.$9#$b#Hm? No, we're not treating you as a replacement third member or anything. We love you for you.",


// Remi gifts every wednesday during marriage
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.spring.3": "Happy new year!$9#$b#Erm, have I said that already? I can't tell.$6",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.spring.17": "[257]This mushroom smells uncommon. I figured you're into uncommon stuff. You can have it.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.spring.24": "What are you doing here? Aren't you supposed to be at the Flower Dance?$9#$b#You go on now. Fish and I will be having our own flower dance. Hehe...$12#$b#Actually, you could use this sunflower to wear on your hair.[421]$11#$e#What do you mean it's not in season yet?$6#$e#Semi-unrelated but... if you spot a green-haired woman wearing red plaid coming towards you, run the other way.$6",

"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.summer.3": "[259]I found this one in the forest. I know you can make use of this.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.summer.10": "[266]Here, you can have this.#$b#So, wanna have a chat?#$e#What? You wondering where I got that?#$b#I go from place to place and stumble upon things sometimes. Probably from a community farm in another town.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.summer.17": "[88]Coconut!$9#$b#It's getting really warm. I figured there would be ripe coconuts outside of town.#$e#Got time to chat? Got work to do? Either way is fine.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.summer.24": "[90]Have a cactus fruit. Don't prick yourself.#$e#How about you take a break for a bit?",

"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.fall.3": "[613]It's apple season! You can have this sweet-smelling one.$9",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.fall.10": "[637]Pom pom. Hehe, get it?$11#$b#Lame? Yeah, I agree with you.#$e#Got a story to tell? I'll listen.#$b#Yeah, even if I'm deaf I can lend you an ear. I have my ways.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.fall.17": "[194]Decided to go simple and fried an egg. I've been wanting to see if I can still perfect the sunny-side up.#$b#Hope you don't mind a simple breakfast.$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.fall.24": "[348]Wine!$h#$b#This one isn't as aged as the others, but it's ready to drink.#$e#So um, do you drink or... I keep forgetting.$6#$b#You can always give it to someone else if you don't want it.",

"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.winter.3": "[446]Here's a mutilated foot of a small furry animal. The say it's lucky.#$e#...When I heard humans are into this stuff, I kinda gagged.$6#$e#How is it lucky anyways? The practice sounds too awful to be anything good.$7#$e#Sorry. I'm rambling too much.#$b#So, what's your opinion about it?",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.winter.10": "[228]Maki Roll!$9#$b#Thanks for letting me use your kitchen. I've been having a blast cooking with the equipment you got here.",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.winter.17": "[444]Hm? No no, I didn't pluck this off of a poor duck. I found it on the ground outside of town.#$b#Texture's all nice, huh?$11",
"MARRIAGE.remi.wednesdayGift.winter.24": "[445]Here's some fancy-schmancy caviar. Fish is great when it comes to harvesting roes... and pretty much anything fish-related.$11#$e#That would do great with fancy wine.#$e#I also used to brew a lot of alcohol. It's pretty easy when time doesn't matter so much.$11",




// Oarfish Marriage Dialogue
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.patio": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish seems to enjoy the view outside.#$e#...$l#$b#%Oarfish gestures how much the farm fits your personality.#$b#...!$h",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.funLeave": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish seems ready to head out with Remi.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.funReturn": "...!$h#$b#%Oarfish seems satisfied with their outing.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.jobLeave": "...$7#$b#%Oarfish seems ready to head out.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.jobReturn": "...!$h#$b#%Oarfish seems happy to be back home.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.spouseRoom": "[903 728 732 204]...$7#$b#%Oarfish hands you some packed lunch and refreshments for the day.#$e#...$7#$b#%Oarfish resumes on cleaning and organizing her and Remi's collection of loot and knick-knacks. The chain on the wall is completely rust-free...",

"MARRIAGE.oarfish.rainy_day.1": "[903 728 732 204]...$l#$b#%Oarfish gestures you to try not to catch a cold.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.rainy_day.2": "[903 728 732 204]...$7#$b#%Oarfish returns to where she was scaling a fish. So that was that fishy smell...",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.rainy_day.3": "[903 728 732 204]...$7#$b#%Oarfish returns to the blanket where she was snuggled in.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.rainy_day.4": "[903 728 732 204]...$7#$b#%Oarfish resumes watching the rain from a window.",
"MARRIAGE.oarfish.rainy_day.5": "[903 728 732 204]...$7#$b#%Oarfish returns to where she was poking Remi.",
